[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-851 flagship-parity promotion (DatomicStore + pricing + billing)" "pricing-intel run pricing-intel-20260722-01" "Managed School Ops (Starter) Stripe live objects"], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-851-primary-education-flagship-parity", :adr/related ["adr-2607152900" "adr-2607161745" "adr-2607172600" "adr-2607189300" "cloud-itonami-isic-851"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607220200-cloud-itonami-isic-851-primary-education-flagship-parity", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-22", :adr/body "# ADR-2607220200: cloud-itonami-isic-851 (Primary Education) -- flagship-parity promotion: DatomicStore + pricing-intel run 20260722-01 + Managed School Ops (Starter) Stripe live Payment Link\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-22\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive 2026-07-22: bring cloud-itonami-isic-851 to the same\nreal, evidenced flagship state as isic-6399/6310/7810/5820, scoped explicitly to the proven\npattern -- store parity + business-model.md + live Stripe Payment Link -- not a novel bespoke\nAPI/claim-page buildout beyond what any existing flagship has; agent-executed)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-851` (2 child commits, no actor-behavior\nchanges), superproject `90-docs/pricing-intelligence/`, `90-docs/business/`, Stripe live account.\n**Builds on**: ADR-2607152900 (isic-851's own original design/implementation ADR), ADR-2607161745\n(flagship Managed-tier Stripe pattern, original 3-flagship cohort), ADR-2607172600 (isic-5820\nflagship promotion, same pattern one cohort member earlier)\n\n## Context\n\nA prior investigation in this same session found that ISIC-85 (education) has 14\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` repos registered `:implemented` in `kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry, but\nevery one of them is a MemStore-only, no-pricing-doc, no-billing OSS blueprint -- \"implemented\"\nmeant test-covered code, not anything with a real-money path. The owner then asked to bring one\nconcrete actor (`cloud-itonami-isic-851`, Pre-primary and Primary Education) to a state that\nactually operates on a real-customer/real-data premise.\n\nInvestigating the EXISTING flagship cohort (6399/6310/7810/5820) first, to avoid inventing new\narchitecture: none of the four have a dedicated backend API, a persistent-by-default store, or a\nvertical-specific claim/onboarding page. All four are static GitHub Pages sites + a no-code Stripe\nPayment Link, with `MemStore` remaining the default store and a `DatomicStore` protocol\nimplementation existing only as a swap-in option, never actually pointed at a live database. All\nfour sit at \"Business=2\" in `cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`'s cohort table: Payment Link\nlive, zero paid tenants. Given this, the owner chose (via AskUserQuestion) the proven, evidenced\nscope over a novel bespoke-API/claim-page buildout that no existing flagship has.\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-851` itself had a real gap even relative to that modest bar: unlike\n6399/6310/7810, its `schoolops.store` had no `DatomicStore` at all (MemStore-only), and it had no\n`docs/business-model.md` and no Stripe billing object (flagship checklist items 5 and 7 of\nADR-2607189300's 7-item checklist, per the existing `cloud-itonami-flagship-checklist-scan.edn`\nscan). Items 2/4/6 were already closed (nightly build-time-regenerated demo console, per the\nADR-2607189300 Wave5 seq6 generator-template proof).\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. `DatomicStore` added to `schoolops.store` (store parity, no behavior change)\n\nMirrors `cloud-itonami-isic-7810`'s `employmentops.store` pattern exactly: `langchain.db`-backed,\nEDN-string-encoded compound values, `:student/id`/`:ledger/seq`/`:coordination-record/seq` as\n`:db.unique/identity` schema attrs. `store_contract_test.clj` extended with a `backends` helper\nproving both `MemStore` and `DatomicStore` satisfy the identical `Store` protocol contract. Ran\n43 tests / 146 assertions / 0 failures (`clojure -M:dev:test`, up from 40/119 at ADR-2607152900);\n`clj-kondo`: 0 errors, 0 warnings. Merged to main (`e6f1901` -> `fe65154`). This closes the actual\ngap that would block \"real data\": before this, there was no swap-in path to a persistent backend\nat all for this specific actor.\n\n### 2. `pricing-intelligence` run `pricing-intel-20260722-01` (obs seq 137-141, rec seq 142)\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-851` was outside the original 28-vertical pilot batch (like 6399/7810/5820\nbefore their own follow-up runs) and had zero pricing research. Five real competitors surveyed\n2026-07-22: SchoolCues ($75/mo base + up to $1/mo/student, vendor's own blog, direct site fetch\nblocked by bot-protection -- captured via search synthesis, marked `:tier/estimated` accordingly),\nBloomz ($3/student/year schoolwide, published directly on Bloomz's own comparison blog, marked\n`:tier/published`), and three fully sales-gated products with zero public pricing anywhere --\nParentSquare, Brightwheel, Procare (`:tier/opaque`). An earlier search pass surfaced an unverified\n\"$3,600/year for up to 600 students\" ParentSquare figure; two follow-up direct fetches of pages\nthat should have contained it did not reproduce that number, so it was deliberately NOT recorded\nas an observation -- logged only as a negative-result note in the ledger's ParentSquare\nobservation, to avoid propagating an unconfirmed number.\n\nRecommended band: **¥15,000-40,000/月 flat per school**, converting the 2 published anchors\nat ~¥150/$ for an illustrative 300-student primary school (Bloomz ~¥11,000/月; SchoolCues at\nfull modular buildout ~¥56,000/月), biased low because isic-851 is coordination-only (no\nparent-broadcast messaging, no tuition/payment processing, no gradebook/SIS) versus either\ncomp's full suite -- but carrying a structural governance guarantee neither comp has (permanent\nHARD block on non-`:propose` effects and out-of-scope content; safety-concern flags can never\nauto-commit at any rollout phase). **This band is deliberately NOT the ¥50,000-150,000/月\nportfolio-uniform range** used by 6399/6310/7810/5820 -- that range was anchored on HR/\nrecruiting/CRM per-seat SaaS competitors with no evidenced relationship to K-12 school\nadministrative-coordination pricing; carrying it over without market evidence would be exactly\nthe kind of unfounded figure this ledger exists to prevent.\n\nBoth `pricing-intelligence.datoms.edn` (new `:vertical/isic-851` catalog entry + 5 new\n`:product/*` entries) and `pricing-intelligence-ledger.edn` (6 new append-only facts) re-verified\nqueryable end-to-end via the documented `query.clj` harness from outside the superproject tree:\n27 schema attrs, 141 catalog entities (up from 116), 142 ledger events (up from 118) -> 1568\ndatoms transacted successfully.\n\n### 3. Stripe live objects -- Managed School Ops (Starter), ¥25,000/月 flat\n\nSame account and procedure as ADR-2607161745/ADR-2607172600 (`op read` into a shell variable\nonce inside a single non-echoing command, value never printed or logged; Idempotency-Key on\nevery call; flat `recurring[interval]=month` Price, no Billing Meter; temp files holding the\nkey/API responses deleted immediately after use):\n\n- Product `prod_UvobXmKuNqBNeR` \"Managed School Ops (Starter)\"\n- Price `price_1TvwyFBcblPoapUJNjSK4Fks` (JPY 25,000/month recurring, unlimited staff seats)\n- Payment Link `plink_1TvwyKBcblPoapUJGEJVcVAf` -> https://buy.stripe.com/bJe3cu74ncW46qs5c3bMQ0h\n  (verified live via a real HTTP GET, returned 200)\n\nRecorded in 1Password (`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami flagship Managed-tier Stripe Payment Links`, new\n`isic-851 product`/`isic-851 price`/`isic-851 payment-link`/`isic-851 note` fields -- the note\nfield flags that this is NOT the shared ¥80,000/月 template price, unlike every other entry in\nthat same 1Password item). Published in the child repo's new `docs/business-model.md` (server-\nside merge `a9e3cf1` -> `c588be3`); the stale generic-template `isco-1212` claim-funnel link in\n`docs/operator-quickstart.md` (isco-1212 is a DIFFERENT vertical's own HR-signup page, never\nwired to isic-851) was replaced with a Production Posture section pointing at the DatomicStore\nswap and the new business-model.md, mirroring isic-7810's quickstart shape. The\noperator-interest issue template (mirrored from isic-7810) was added so the Subscribe link's\nfollow-up path actually resolves.\n\n**No school has claimed or subscribed to this tier. This ADR does not create a paying customer --\nit creates a real, working, live-money checkout with zero paid tenants, and says so explicitly in\nevery place the price appears** (business-model.md, this ADR, the 1Password note field).\n\n### 4. Flagship cohort table (no actor code in this ADR)\n\n`cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`'s \"Education\" cohort row (previously Design 4 / Impl-core 4\n/ Impl-product 1 / Business 0, \"Full modules; no product face\") is superseded by a new,\nisic-851-specific flagship row: Design 4 / Impl-core 4 / Impl-product 4 (demo + quickstart +\npricing docs, mirroring the near-flagship 7810 shape) / Business 2 (Payment Link live, no paid\norg yet -- same Business formula as every other cohort member). The other 13 ISIC-85 repos are\nUNCHANGED by this ADR -- they remain exactly where the earlier investigation found them: real,\ntested, governed OSS blueprints with no pricing docs and no billing object. Promoting them is a\nseparate decision this ADR does not make.\n\n## Consequences / open gates\n\n- First-paid-org gate unchanged: `hyp/itonami-smb-pay` stays `measuring`; isic-851 adds a 5th\n  live link to the same unclosed gate.\n- E2E checkout verification remains open (inherited from ADR-2607161620), now for 5 flagship\n  links, not 4.\n- The other 13 ISIC-85 repos (852/853/854/855/8510/8521/8522/8530/8541/8542/8549/8550/8569)\n  remain non-flagship, MemStore-only OSS blueprints -- explicitly not promoted by this ADR.\n- The ¥15k-40k/月 education band is a NEW, narrower pattern in this portfolio (the first\n  vertical whose real-market research landed meaningfully below the ¥50k-150k/月\n  portfolio-uniform range) -- future education-adjacent verticals (isic-8550 already has its own\n  distinct tutoring-market pricing-intel row) should anchor against real research per vertical,\n  not assume portfolio uniformity applies to every cluster.\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-22", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607220200: cloud-itonami-isic-851 (Primary Education) -- flagship-parity promotion: DatomicStore + pricing-intel run 20260722-01 + Managed School Ops (Starter) Stripe live Payment Link", :adr/source-format "edn"}]
